 MNEMONICS 	          EXPLANATION 
MVI A, 0FFH	          moves the value 9A (in hexadecimal) into register A.
ANI 80H	              performs a bitwise AND operation between the accumulator (A) and 80H
JZ POSITIVE	          instruction checks the Zero flag.
MVI B, 01H	          the jump to NEG was not taken, this instruction moves the immediate value 22H (34 in decimal) into register A.
JMP STORE	            instruction causes an unconditional jump to the label ST0.
POSITIVE: MVI B, 00H	        The jump to NEG had been taken (if ANI resulted in zero), this instruction would have moved 11H (17 in decimal) into register A.
STORE: MOV A, B	       Store the accumulator content at memory location 8051
STA 3000	              STORE DATA OF AACCUMULATOR 
HLT	                    Halt the process 
